# Marketing SPA build-time configuration.
# Copy to `.env` for local overrides. Vite only exposes vars prefixed VITE_.

# Base URL for the SelahCue account API.
#
# LEAVE THIS UNSET unless you know you need it. Empty means the SPA calls a RELATIVE
# `/graphql/account` and is therefore SAME-ORIGIN with the API — proxied by the Vite dev
# server (see vite.config.ts) and by nginx in production (see nginx.conf). Three things
# depend on staying same-origin:
#
#   1. No CORS. The API reads CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS from env but `corsheaders` is in
#      neither INSTALLED_APPS nor MIDDLEWARE, so it emits no CORS headers today.
#   2. The account session cookie is SameSite=Strict, so a browser never sends it on a
#      cross-site request. The sign-in and account-portal work depends on it arriving.
#   3. Django's CSRF check wants an Origin that matches.
#
# Setting this to an absolute origin requires all three to be solved first (86ak11r67).
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Where the Vite dev server proxies /graphql to. Not a VITE_ var — it is read by
# vite.config.ts at startup, never shipped to the browser.
# SELAHCUE_API_ORIGIN=http://localhost:8008
